-- title:
--   Ogg's modular unit lies in the full level-N function field
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number. Write $\Delta =$ [`ModularCurve.deltaSeries`](def/ModularCurve_ModularUnit.html#L107) for the Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$ given by $q$ (the Hahn series $q^{1}$ with coefficient $1$) times the power series `dedekindEtaUnitQ`, and for $d \ge 1$ let `qExpand ℚ d` denote the substitution $q \mapsto q^{d}$ on `LaurentSeries ℚ`. The theorem asserts that the element
--   [`ModularCurve.modularUnitSeries N`](def/ModularCurve_ModularUnit.html#L127) $= \Delta(q)\cdot \Delta(q^{N})^{-1}$, the product of $\Delta$ with the inverse of its $N$-th $q$-expansion `deltaSeriesN N`, belongs to [`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldFull N`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L305), namely the intermediate field of `LaurentSeries ℚ` over $\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the set of all series $\mathrm{qExpand}_{\mathbb{Q},d}(\mathtt{jq})$ for nonzero divisors $d$ of $N$, i.e. by the $q$-expansions $j(q^{d})$, $d \mid N$. No primality or other hypothesis on $N$ is imposed: the assertion is unconditional in the level.
--
--   This is the statement that Ogg's modular unit $\Delta(q)/\Delta(q^{N})$ is a rational function of the expansions $j(q^{d})$, $d \mid N$, at arbitrary, not merely prime, level; in the formalisation it supplies the unit used to produce functions with prescribed divisors on the modular curve of level $N$. It is cited throughout the construction of Deligne–Rapoport-style models and charts at general level.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_modularUnitSeries_mem_modularFunctionFieldFull.lean

